            {
                "entry_id": "ae939e85-20b5-317d-91bd-03236f10339a",
                "word": "bipède",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c8325d43-31c9-40fc-9320-11e9e95c6aad",
                        "entry_id": "ae939e85-20b5-317d-91bd-03236f10339a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bipèdes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4fbaa96c-5709-37dd-8fc2-166bc9b8aa72",
                        "entry_id": "ae939e85-20b5-317d-91bd-03236f10339a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Animal qui marche sur deux pattes, plus spécifiquement les êtres humains."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "44b40202-c588-4085-8712-72a102e9c254",
                                "sense_id": "4fbaa96c-5709-37dd-8fc2-166bc9b8aa72",
                                "text": "Si je n'avais peur d'être taxé de partialité pour l'espèce humaine, j'ajouterais que les quadrupèdes sont là beaucoup mieux traités que les bipèdes, attendu qu'ils trouvent dans leur écurie du son, de la paille, de l'avoine et du foin, ce qui équivaut pour eux à un dîner à quatre services, tandis que les bipèdes ne peuvent obtenir dans leur hôtel que du lait, du pain et du vin, ce qui n'équivaut pas même à un mauvais déjeuner."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4b7f604-1304-4c3d-9a42-d0eac12c5f6e",
                                "sense_id": "4fbaa96c-5709-37dd-8fc2-166bc9b8aa72",
                                "text": "Les bêtes cornues, nous ne voulons pas parler des bipèdes mariés qui lors traversaient le Pont-Neuf, mais bien des bœufs, couraient çà et là, baissant la tête, effarés, harcelés par les chiens, bâtonnés par les conducteurs."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a6683e99-d00e-3041-845c-f5e1e22aea13",
                        "entry_id": "ae939e85-20b5-317d-91bd-03236f10339a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ensemble de deux jambes d'un cheval"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "51281260-6305-4e95-a3dc-acb1a75fa67f",
                                "sense_id": "a6683e99-d00e-3041-845c-f5e1e22aea13",
                                "text": "Bipède antérieur."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "96c0603b-4c9b-4230-84d3-eeba3f80c35c",
                                "sense_id": "a6683e99-d00e-3041-845c-f5e1e22aea13",
                                "text": "Bipède latéral."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c4dae25-59e5-4d5d-8646-6d8bfe71c536",
                                "sense_id": "a6683e99-d00e-3041-845c-f5e1e22aea13",
                                "text": "Bipède diagonal."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4c0f4cdd-710d-4cc8-ab0a-3d1884e1cea8",
                        "source_entry_id": "ae939e85-20b5-317d-91bd-03236f10339a",
                        "target_lang_word": "Zweibeiner",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Zweibeiner",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7633360a-aa6d-3b10-a4db-6157c40207b2",
                                        "entry_id": "2d2a9106-e7d2-3af2-8a0c-57a35984be2e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lebewesen mit zwei Beinen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "641198b4-8c74-4d08-a69f-ef4b24cea0af",
                                                "sense_id": "7633360a-aa6d-3b10-a4db-6157c40207b2",
                                                "text": "„Er war Nordstaatler, hatte die sieben Meere befahren und alles mitgemacht, was einem flügellosen Zweibeiner auf dieser Erde passieren kann.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ca2dc09f-4809-46c5-90e5-7aba7bcf9115",
                        "source_entry_id": "ae939e85-20b5-317d-91bd-03236f10339a",
                        "target_lang_word": "Zweifüßler",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c96d42b0-d4e8-437a-8262-3cc8b3144ea4",
                        "source_entry_id": "ae939e85-20b5-317d-91bd-03236f10339a",
                        "target_lang_word": "biped",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "biped",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79cf95f1-b03a-32c1-961e-fd9d4441ba26",
                                        "entry_id": "981d18f7-bb26-3450-ab6b-e877e1f2a5ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An animal, being, or construction that goes about on two feet (or two legs)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cdefd12-e52f-4f38-b4c3-95dec8251f1b",
                                                "sense_id": "79cf95f1-b03a-32c1-961e-fd9d4441ba26",
                                                "text": "He was badgered in that witness-box for an hour. By a distracting repetition of cross-examination he was forced to confess that he had seen and spoken to a human biped in broad daylight, yet could not recollect one singularity to distinguish this phantom from the flat mass of humanity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7dd6cd7c-51f3-4aed-a8e2-04ef52947cec",
                                                "sense_id": "79cf95f1-b03a-32c1-961e-fd9d4441ba26",
                                                "text": "Luján, or, rather, the biped which used to be Luján, walks right up to him. He is a little shorter than Wheeler, but much heavier-set. Rooted to the spot, not thinking clearly, Wheeler holds his violin up, as if this will shield him. The conductor takes the instrument from his unresisting hands and breaks its neck underfoot, perfunctorily, as if crushing a box for recycling."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
